Backport of upstream df94112ceebf ("drm/amd/display: Gate HDMI FRL status
polling on active FRL link rate", Fangzhi Zuo, in 7.3) to 7.2.

connector_signal is never SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL, so the 200 ms FRL status poll
skipped every link: a late FRL_Start was never acknowledged and FLT_Update
never retrained a running link.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -2024,7 +2024,7 @@
 		if (!dc_is_hdmi_signal(dc_link->connector_signal))
 			continue;
 
-		if (dc_link->connector_signal != SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_FRL)
+		if (dc_link->frl_link_settings.frl_link_rate == 0)
 			continue;
 
 		link_update = dc_link_frl_poll_status_flag(dc_link);
